# PIXELTRUTH Development Phases

## Status convention

Use NOT STARTED, IN PROGRESS, BLOCKED, or COMPLETE. A phase is COMPLETE only when its exit criteria are met, required tests pass, documentation is updated, and the user receives a report. Do not start a phase until its explicit START PHASE command is received.

## Current status

- Phase 0 — COMPLETE (2026-11-25). The user explicitly authorized a greenfield foundation. Python 3.11.0 was confirmed; the existing project-local environment was verified; the requested scaffold, documentation, starter Streamlit entry point, README, license notice, and gitignore were created; and local main/develop branches were prepared without a remote. No forensic features were implemented. See memory.in for environment details.
- Phase 1 — COMPLETE (2026-11-25). Implemented content-based upload validation, bounded decoding, image properties, common EXIF fields/statuses, SHA-256, and a working single-image Streamlit inspection view. Rechecks fixed valid EXIF orientation labels being marked invalid and stopped reporting palette images as reliably 8-bit per channel. At Phase 1 completion, XMP/IPTC parsing was unsupported; the later Phase 2 metadata-support extension added the formats and storage locations listed below. GPS, integrity findings, comparison, ELA, histograms, assessment, and PDF reports were still to come at that milestone.
- Phase 2 — COMPLETE (2026-11-25). Added structured metadata availability/validity findings, timestamp and EXIF dimension consistency checks, on-demand GPS reveal/clear behavior, two-image property/hash/metadata comparison with a bounded sampled RGB difference indicator, and XMP/IPTC extraction. XMP locations: JPEG APP1, PNG `XML:com.adobe.xmp` text chunks, WebP `XMP ` RIFF chunks, TIFF tag 700. IPTC locations: JPEG Photoshop APP13 `8BIM` resource 0x0404, TIFF tag 33723. JPEG Extended XMP is detected but not reassembled; a standard packet is retained with a limitation note when present. Rechecked with 65 passing tests, including six focused AppTest cases and one complete AppTest flow; pip check, diff check, and local app health/page checks pass. The earlier AppTest timeout did not reproduce and its cause is unknown. AppTest renders all four tabs but does not expose tab selection; actual tab switching is not covered. No assessment verdict or authenticity score was added; those remain Phase 3.
- Phase 3 — IN PROGRESS. Phase 3.1 (JPEG-only ELA) and Phase 3.2 (RGB histograms) are COMPLETE; Phase 3.3 (assessment and findings integration) is NOT STARTED.
- Phase 4 — NOT STARTED.
- Phase 5 — NOT STARTED.

## Phase 0 — Inspection and preparation

Authorization command: START PHASE 0

Tasks:
- Inspect the actual repository structure, Git status/branches, and all project documents.
- Check Python 3.11 availability and inspect requirements.txt without installing packages.
- Review existing source and test structure, if present.
- Identify missing files, dependency conflicts, architectural fit, and technical risks.
- Prepare a scoped implementation plan and report.

Exit criteria:
- Correct project checkout is available and its status is understood.
- Required documents and source of truth are read and reconciled.
- Proposed plan and risks are reported; unresolved decisions are identified.
- No implementation starts unless separately authorized by the relevant phase command.

## Phase 1 — Image inspection foundation

Authorization command: START PHASE 1

Tasks: upload validation; content-based format detection; safe decode and resource limits; image properties; metadata extraction/statuses; SHA-256 over original bytes.

Exit criteria: supported formats are validated and tested; malformed, corrupt, unsupported, and oversized inputs return clear outcomes; properties and metadata statuses are accurate; hash matches original bytes; UI state is connected without permanent storage by default.

## Phase 2 — Metadata intelligence

Authorization command: START PHASE 2

Tasks: metadata integrity and consistency rules; structured findings; gated GPS and session clearing; two-image comparison and supported similarity measures.

Exit criteria: rules are deterministic and explained; missing metadata alone does not imply manipulation; GPS is hidden until requested and excluded from report defaults; comparison distinguishes hashes from visual similarity; tests cover edge cases.

## Phase 3 — Forensic analysis

Authorization command: START PHASE 3

Tasks: documented JPEG-only ELA; RGB histograms; deterministic assessment engine; findings and explanation presentation.

Exit criteria: unsupported formats do not receive ELA; analyses expose method and limitations; assessment is one of the three allowed labels with documented rules; no fake scores or authenticity claims; tests cover applicability and rules.

### Phase 3.1 — JPEG-only Error Level Analysis

Authorization: The user explicitly requested “implement Phase 3.1” on 2026-11-25 after reviewing the project documentation and architecture.

Scope: JPEG-only one-pass recompression residual, adjustable quality and display scale, a bounded core result, Streamlit side-by-side view, and tests. This subphase does not include histograms, assessments, or assessment-driven findings.

Exit criteria: content-detected JPEG only; non-JPEG and invalid inputs are handled safely; resource limits are enforced before full decode; method and limitations are shown; results remain in session state and are cleared when the input or parameters change; tests pass.

### Phase 3.2 — RGB histograms

Authorization: The user authorized Phase 3 and specified Phase 3.2 (RGB histograms) on 2026-11-25.

Scope: Opt-in 256-bin RGB intensity histograms for supported validated images, a pooled channel-value distribution, labeled separate channel views in monochrome styles, and clear method/limitations. No assessment, verdict, or authenticity score is part of this subphase.

Exit criteria: supported images are validated before counting; all frames and counted values are clearly described; chart axes and channel labels are clear; analysis is opt-in and resource-bounded; tests pass; documentation is updated.

Status: COMPLETE. Counts from every frame are pooled and labeled; the UI is opt-in and uses the existing Plotly dependency with monochrome line styles. See the Phase 3.2 completion record below.

### Later Phase 3 subphase

- Phase 3.3 — Deterministic three-state assessment and findings integration.

## Phase 4 — Reporting

Authorization command: START PHASE 4

Tasks: PDF report content/layout; selected sections; report ID/date; privacy redaction and GPS exclusion; report generation validation.

Exit criteria: report reflects actual analysis and user-selected sections; GPS is excluded by default; limitations/methods/hash are present; no unintended local paths or sensitive values leak; tests validate generated report content.

## Phase 5 — Integration and quality assurance

Authorization command: START PHASE 5

Tasks: integration; macOS/Windows checks; privacy and security review; performance and resource checks; bug fixes; documentation and demonstration readiness.

Exit criteria: end-to-end supported workflows function; relevant test suite passes; platform-specific issues are resolved or documented; privacy defaults are verified; documentation and known limitations are current; final report is delivered.

## Phase completion record

